    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d135">

                <pb facs="0191" n="1025" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1025"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112A/991</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Birch</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-26T18:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 26, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>252. Report present status of enemy firms Portugal on British statutory list and
                    actual progress made by Portuguese Government <pb facs="0192" n="1026"
                        xml:id="pg1026"/> in liquidating enemy interest therein. Prepare to report
                    on such houses or other enemy firms for inclusion American enemy trading list.
                    Proper to informally intimate to Portuguese Government such American listing
                    under consideration unless definite assurance received prompt liquidation by
                    present Government of enemy interest.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
